Z||000005||Cooter||02-11-2001||02:43 PM||||An old trick for a cheap stall converter for a v8 was to use a 4 cyl Vega converter. It stands to reason that the same would apply to the v6 using a 4 cyl converter. The more torque you feed the 4 cyl converter, the more it will stall. With the Vega converter in my big block chevelle it would stall at about 4,000 but behind my 350 it only stalled to 2,500.||||reg||1
